{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The well, which the princes dug.</b> They are Moses and Aaron, and Scripture calls them 'princes' and 'nobles of the people' because they dug it and hewed it with their staffs, with which they struck. And since Scripture set them both equal in the digging of it, therefore it was necessary to mention 'the lawgiver' — that is, Moses — to say that after the well disappeared with the death of Miriam, it returned only by the merit of the lawgiver." "<b>And from the wilderness, a gift.</b> From the wilderness, which is a land of drought and thirst, He gave us such a great gift — and it is the gift of the well; and from this gift they came to the streams of Arnon, where all the great miracles were performed for them. And so the entire language of the song is a recounting of the mercies of the Holy One, blessed be He, and the goodnesses that He did greatly for Israel. And from the streams of Arnon they came to Bamoth — that is, to the wars against Sihon and Og, who were mighty kings, and Scripture calls them 'heights' (במות); and from Bamoth in the valley to the top of the peak that looks out upon the face of the land, which is all wasteland, a howling desert, in which there is no wadi other than this one." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> 'Then Israel sang this song' — it should have said 'they sang this song to YHWH,' and should also have mentioned the name of Moses, just as we find in the Song at the Sea. But because Moses was punished on account of this well, and because of it it was decreed upon him that he not enter the land, therefore the name of Moses is not mentioned in this song — for this song is a narration of praises of the well, and since Moses was punished through it, how could he praise it? A person does not praise the one who caused him harm. And since the name of Moses is not mentioned, the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, is not mentioned either. To what may the matter be compared? To a king who was invited to a feast. He said: If my beloved is there, I am going there; and if my beloved is not there, I am not going."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:42.357311391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}